        conclusions:
          "5. Conclusion: The nuclear lamina is the physical nexus where genome mechanics, epigenetic silencing, and innate immunity converge. Both accelerated progeroid syndromes and normal human chronological aging share a common pathological pathway: accumulation of cryptically spliced farnesylated Progerin and depletion of Lamin B1/SIRT7/WRN destabilize the inner nuclear membrane, allow hyper-acetylated microtubules to deform the nucleus via the SUN1 LINC complex, and untether H3K9me3 Lamina-Associated Domains, unleashing satellite RNA transcription and LINE-1/cGAS-STING inflammation. The demonstration that in vivo Adenine Base Editing (ABE) rescues aortic VSMC dropout and extends HGPS mouse lifespan by 140% to normal old age — complemented by cryptic splice-switching ASOs, NAT10/Remodelin mechanotransduction blockade, and SIRT7/WRN heterochromatin stabilization — provides a blueprint for preserving nuclear envelope integrity across the human lifespan.",
