        conclusions:
          "4. Conclusion: Whole-organ bioengineering has progressed from conceptual aspiration to three actionable engineering tracks: (1) in the near term, 69-gene CRISPR-edited porcine organs (`3KO.7HT.RI`) abolish hyperacute rejection, coagulation incompatibility, and retroviral risk, achieving >2-year survival in primates and clinical translation in humans; (2) in the medium term, perfusion-decellularized whole-organ ECM scaffolds preserve 100% of nature's microvascular and basement-membrane architecture and are entering ex vivo and implantable human trials when re-endothelialized with human cells; and (3) in the long term, the convergence of SLATE food-dye projection stereolithography (printing entangled capillary/alveolar networks) with SWIFT sacrificial vascular writing inside 200-million-cell/mL iPSC organoid matrices charts the path to patient-specific, immunosuppression-free replacement hearts, kidneys, lungs, and livers.",
